    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "manual",
      "desc": "Part (b) rubric: swapping x and y leaves the relation unchanged, so the curve is symmetric about the line y = x. The point (3,3) lies on that line, so reflecting the curve in y = x sends the tangent there to itself; a reflection in y = x turns a slope m into 1/m, so m must equal 1/m and therefore m is 1 or -1. It cannot be 1, because that is the direction of the mirror line itself and the curve crosses that line rather than touching it, leaving -1. Full credit needs the symmetry observation and the conclusion that the slope is its own reciprocal. Award partial credit for noticing the symmetry alone.",
      "slot": "(b) the symmetry argument",
      "skill": "product-and-chain-in-implicit",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "bloom": "justify",
      "standard": "FUN-3.D"
    }
